      "context_type": "paragraph",
      "title_en": "Bal Gandharva",
      "content_en": "Bal Gandharva, whose real name was Narayan Shripad Rajhans, was born on 26 June 1888 in Narayangaon, Maharashtra. He was a celebrated Marathi theatre actor and singer, famous for playing female roles with extraordinary grace. His melodious voice and exceptional acting skills earned him the title 'Bal Gandharva' — meaning 'Child of the Heavenly Singers'. He was associated with the Kirloskar Natak Company. His performances in plays like 'Sharada', 'Manapman', and 'Saubhadra' are legendary. He is considered one of the greatest artists in the history of Marathi theatre.",
      "applies_from": 1,
      "applies_to": 5
    },
    {
      "context_type": "poem",
      "title_en": "The Brook",
      "content_en": "Down the mountain, down the hill,\nThe little brook runs never still.\nOver pebbles, stones and sand,\nIt flows to reach the distant land.\nThe birds they sing, the flowers bloom,\nThe little brook dispels all gloom.\nIt waters fields and quenches thirst,\nOf all living things, it serves them first.",
      "applies_from": 6,
      "applies_to": 8
    },
